Oil is found only in the ground, while gas can also be produced by decaying organic matter. Gas is better for the environment than oil, especially in terms of greenhouse gas emissions. However, heating oil systems have a longer lifespan than gas furnaces, with an average life expectancy of 30 years or more if properly maintained, compared to 11-14 years for gas furnaces.

